{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BringsSurface.PentagonTwistAssociator","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.PentagonTwistAssociator","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Abel"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.PentagonTwist.assoc_pentagon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.PentagonTwist.assoc_pentagon","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/PentagonTwistAssociator.lean#L50-L59","doc":"**Pentagon holds automatically for a twist associator (`d² = 0`).**\nFor any 2-cochain twist, the associator `α = dF` satisfies the pentagon /\n3-cocycle identity. This is the mechanism by which turning on a graded twist\n(the octonion `(ℤ/2)³` cochain) breaks strict associativity while preserving Mac\nLane coherence — the categorical form of \"deform the pentagon.\" ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.PentagonTwist.assoc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.PentagonTwist.assoc","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/PentagonTwistAssociator.lean#L44-L48","doc":"Associator of a 2-cochain twist `F` (`e_a·e_b = F(a,b) · e_{a+b}`, phases\nadditive): the \"defect\" `(e_a·e_b)·e_c − e_a·(e_b·e_c)`, i.e. the coboundary\n`dF`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}